  "analysis": "Comparing candidate platforms against RefractRouter v0.1 selection criteria reveals a clear tradeoff between harness maturity, typed-output guarantees, and validation isolation. DeepAgents (source_001) offers the richest agent-harness feature set—planning, sub-agents, filesystem abstraction, and human-in-the-loop controls—but its autonomous planning and dynamic sub-agent generation are explicitly disabled for v0.1, meaning much of its value is unused in the fixed-DAG execution context. LangGraph (source_002) provides the lower-level graph state machine substrate with durable state and check-pointing, which aligns directly with the fixed task DAG requirement; it is the execution backbone, but lacks higher-level agent conveniences. Pydantic AI (source_003) supplies typed tool definitions and structured outputs, which could improve reliability of per-node model selection results, yet it is not a core dependency unless structured-output parsing becomes a bottleneck—an optional enhancement rather than a foundational choice. DeepSeek Harness (source_004) is architecturally interesting because the agent loop itself is a plugin, but it is reserved for the outer validation environment, not the core routing loop, so it cannot serve as the primary platform without violating the v0.1 boundary. The key tradeoff is between adopting a feature-rich harness (DeepAgents) that must be constrained, versus building directly on a minimal substrate (LangGraph) that matches the fixed-DAG requirement with less overhead. A secondary tradeoff concerns benchmark fidelity: the routing benchmark (source_007) requires fixed DAGs, multiple candidate models, per-node scoring, cost accounting, and critical-path latency, which favors a platform that exposes per-node control and instrumentation—LangGraph's explicit nodes and edges align better than DeepAgents' higher-level abstractions. The scoring rubric (source_008) weights evidence accuracy and analysis depth, so the platform choice must also support reproducible run records and versioned prompts. The research gap (source_005) underscores that per-node model selection is the core question, and static decomposition belongs to the application layer (source_006), meaning the platform should not impose dynamic re-splitting. Overall, LangGraph as the execution substrate with DeepAgents as a constrained harness layer represents the most defensible v0.1 choice, while Pydantic AI remains a conditional add-on and DSH stays outside the core loop.",
