      "claim": "DeepSeek Harness (DSH) is an agent harness where the agent loop itself is a plugin, and for RefractRouter v0.1 DSH is reserved for the outer validation environment, not the core routing loop."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "source_005",
      "title": "LLM routing research gap",
      "content_hash": "418b6cda722a8338f10fa145fb4f4f5c3f188ff413651e4d73aa2949b4e07460",
      "claim": "Existing LLM routing work mostly selects one model for an entire request, while RefractRouter studies whether selecting a model separately for each node in a task DAG can improve the quality-cost-latency Pareto frontier."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "source_006",
      "title": "Task decomposition boundary",
      "content_hash": "96a837f9788f5d0c6d9ab2cc9633775c42dc5569afc70b1782dc1d6d7a198504",
      "claim": "Static task decomposition belongs to the application layer; the router receives the DAG as input and focuses on per-node model selection, with dynamic re-splitting deferred until node-level routing is validated."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "source_007",
      "title": "Benchmark design",
